Job Description:﻿

﻿We are looking for a Senior Data Consultant to join a fast-paced and collaborative environment. In this role, you will design and implement scalable solutions within the Salesforce Data Cloud platform, working closely with stakeholders to translate business needs into technical solutions. 

You will also be responsible for optimizing data models, maintaining integrations with external systems, troubleshooting platform issues, and ensuring high standards for code quality and documentation. This is a great opportunity for professionals who enjoy solving complex data challenges and building impactful Salesforce solutions.

Locations:

- Brazil

- Colombia

- Argentina

- Peru

- Uruguay

- Costa Rica

- Mexico

Requirements:

- 3 years of commercial experience with Salesforce stack;

- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field; 

- 1+ year of proven experience in implementing solutions on Salesforce Data Cloud\CDP Platforms; 

- Experience in integrating Data Cloud with external systems; 

- Hands-on experience with all aspects of salesforce data cloud such as data ingestion, data mapping, identity resolution,SQL queries, segments, etc.; 

- Hands-on experience with the creation of data transformation; 

- Hands-on experience with generating calculated; 

- Solid understanding of DC integration capabilities and ability to work with DC API on projects; 

- Good understanding of Data Cloud credit consumption model; 

- Proficiency in SQL. 

Nice to have: 

- Experience in leading client workshops; 

- Certified Accredited Professional in Salesforce Data Cloud; 

- Experience in developing Salesforce Marketing Cloud; 

- Good understanding of the marketing concepts and overall flow in the marketing automation space;

- Hands-on experience with Agentforce, including a deep understanding of its development workflow and DC components associated with it, such as RAG, Search Index, and unstructured data integration. 

Other skills: 

- English – Excellent written and verbal communication skills; 

- Ability to work in a global multi-cultural multi-national company; 

- Good communication skills and persuasiveness; 

- Ability to lead conversations with both technical and business representatives; 

- Proven ability to work both independently and as a part of an international project team.

Job Responsibilities:

- Create and implement solutions on the Salesforce Data Cloud platform;

- Work with stakeholders to collect requirements and transform them into technical specifications;

- Optimize and maintain data models, ensuring integrity on the Salesforce platform;

- Build and upkeep integrations between Salesforce and external systems;

- Offer technical support and perform troubleshooting for Salesforce Data Cloud applications;

- Document the development process and uphold code quality standards.

What We Offer:

- Competitive salary;

- 100% remote opportunity;

- Paid time off (PTO), sick leave, and national holidays. Benefits will be communicated during the application process depending on your location;

- Travel expenses are covered when applicable;

- Referral program;

- Paid certification program;

- Personal development plan (PDP);

- Access to the language platform.

